{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01Lcs19cLnPDhhCRBVRmb4Wf","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t//! Retrieval V1 benchmark harness and metrics snapshot writer.\n2\t//!\n3\t//! This module follows the existing `cargo test -- --include-ignored` benchmark\n4\t//! convention used elsewhere in the repo. No separate CLI hook is added because\n5\t//! the current benchmark scaffolding is test-first and the task verification\n6\t//! only requires the ignored test entry points.\n7\t//!\n8\t//! `BenchmarkMetrics` is the checked-in schema for\n9\t//! `docs/plans/2026-05-16-cognitive-workspace-fork-build/baselines/retrieval_v1_metrics.json`.\n10\t//! Every field below is produced from the hermetic golden corpus and tightened\n11\t//! only when a new real baseline run improves the metric without relaxing any\n12\t//! other guardrail from `## Phase 4: Retrieval V1` or `## Phase 9: Metrics And\n13\t//! Evaluation`.\n14\t//!\n15\t//! - `corpus_size`: number of golden tasks exercised. Threshold: must equal the\n16\t//!   curated corpus length exactly; tighten by increasing only when new task\n17\t//!   coverage is added to the corpus.\n18\t//! - `top_1_precision`: share of tasks whose first ranked result is relevant.\n19\t//!   Threshold: `1.0`; tighten only by keeping it exact as corpus grows.\n20\t//! - `top_3_precision`: average precision over the first three ranked results.\n21\t//!   Threshold: `>= 0.33`; tighten after a real baseline run proves a higher\n22\t//!   stable floor.\n23\t//! - `top_1_recall`: share of tasks whose relevant set appears in rank one.\n24\t//!   Threshold: `1.0`; tighten only by keeping it exact as corpus grows.\n25\t//! - `top_3_recall`: share of tasks whose relevant set appears somewhere in the\n26\t//!   first three ranked results. Threshold: `1.0`; tighten only by keeping it\n27\t//!   exact as corpus grows.\n28\t//! - `irrelevant_memory_rate`: fraction of top-three memory results that are\n29\t//!   neither the task's golden result nor its expected supporting memory.\n30\t//!   Threshold: `<= 0.17`; tighten when a new baseline produces a lower stable\n31\t//!   ceiling without masking real regressions.\n32\t//! - `mean_rank_of_golden_result`: average one-based rank of the golden result\n33\t//!   before shaping. Threshold: `<= 1.0`; tighten only by keeping the exact\n34\t//!   mean pinned as corpus grows.\n35\t//! - `p50_retrieval_latency_ms`: median end-to-end latency across the corpus.\n36\t//!   Threshold: `<= 50ms`; tighten after a stable faster baseline run.\n37\t//! - `p95_retrieval_latency_ms`: p95 end-to-end latency across the corpus.\n38\t//!   Threshold: `<= 100ms`; tighten after a stable faster baseline run.\n39\t//! - `candidates_per_source`: total ranked candidates per retrieval source.\n40\t//!   Threshold: every source intentionally exercised by the corpus must stay\n41\t//!   `> 0`; tighten by expanding the corpus and then adding more per-source\n42\t//!   lower bounds.\n43\t//! - `dedupe_rate`: fraction of ranked candidates removed by shaper\n44\t//!   deduplication. Threshold: `>= 0.05`; tighten when the corpus proves a\n45\t//!   higher stable minimum.\n46\t//! - `truncation_rate`: fraction of tasks whose shaped bundle truncated.\n47\t//!   Threshold: `0.05..=0.20`; tighten by narrowing the range after a stable\n48\t//!   corpus update.\n49\t\n50\tuse std::collections::BTreeMap;\n51\tuse std::fs;\n52\tuse std::path::{Path, PathBuf};\n53\t\n54\tuse serde::Serialize;\n55\t\n56\tuse crate::retrieval_v1::CandidateSource;\n57\t\n58\tuse super::test_support::{\n59\t    build_fixture, execute_case, golden_cases, ExpectedIdentity, MEMORY_AUTH_VERIFIED,\n60\t    MEMORY_CLI_VERIFIED, MEMORY_CONFIG_VERIFIED, MEMORY_DOCS_VERIFIED,\n61\t    MEMORY_SESSION_VERIFIED,\n62\t};\n63\t\n64\tconst TOP_1_PRECISION_MIN: f64 = 1.0;\n65\tconst TOP_3_PRECISION_MIN: f64 = 0.33;\n66\tconst TOP_1_RECALL_MIN: f64 = 1.0;\n67\tconst TOP_3_RECALL_MIN: f64 = 1.0;\n68\tconst IRRELEVANT_MEMORY_RATE_MAX: f64 = 0.17;\n69\tconst MEAN_RANK_MAX: f64 = 1.0;\n70\tconst P50_LATENCY_MAX_MS: f64 = 50.0;\n71\tconst P95_LATENCY_MAX_MS: f64 = 100.0;\n72\tconst DEDUPE_RATE_MIN: f64 = 0.05;\n73\tconst TRUNCATION_RATE_MIN: f64 = 0.05;\n74\tconst TRUNCATION_RATE_MAX: f64 = 0.20;\n75\t\n76\t#[derive(Debug, Clone, PartialEq, Serialize)]\n77\tstruct BenchmarkMetrics {\n78\t    corpus_size: usize,\n79\t    top_1_precision: f64,\n80\t    top_3_precision: f64,\n81\t    top_1_recall: f64,\n82\t    top_3_recall: f64,\n83\t    irrelevant_memory_rate: f64,\n84\t    mean_rank_of_golden_result: f64,\n85\t    p50_retrieval_latency_ms: f64,\n86\t    p95_retrieval_latency_ms: f64,\n87\t    candidates_per_source: BTreeMap<String, usize>,\n88\t    dedupe_rate: f64,\n89\t    truncation_rate: f64,\n90\t}\n91\t\n92\t#[derive(Default)]\n93\tstruct BenchmarkAccumulator {\n94\t    corpus_size: usize,\n95\t    top1_hits: usize,\n96\t    top3_relevant: usize,\n97\t    irrelevant_memory_hits: usize,\n98\t    top3_slots: usize,\n99\t    total_rank: usize,\n100\t    ranked_total: usize,\n101\t    shaped_total: usize,\n102\t    truncated_total: usize,\n103\t    latencies_ms: Vec<f64>,\n104\t    candidates_per_source: BTreeMap<String, usize>,\n105\t}\n106\t\n107\t#[tokio::test]\n108\t#[ignore]\n109\tasync fn retrieval_v1_benchmark_writes_metrics_snapshot() {\n110\t    let metrics = benchmark_metrics().await;\n111\t    assert_thresholds(&metrics);\n112\t    write_metrics_snapshot(&metrics);\n113\t}\n114\t\n115\t#[tokio::test]\n116\t#[ignore]\n117\tasync fn irrelevant_memory_rate_is_measured_and_regressed() {\n118\t    let metrics = benchmark_metrics().await;\n119\t\n120\t    assert!(metrics.irrelevant_memory_rate <= IRRELEVANT_MEMORY_RATE_MAX);\n121\t}\n122\t\n123\tasync fn benchmark_metrics() -> BenchmarkMetrics {\n124\t    let fixture = build_fixture();\n125\t    let mut acc = BenchmarkAccumulator::default();\n126\t\n127\t    for case in golden_cases() {\n128\t        let run = execute_case(&case, &fixture).await;\n129\t        let relevant = relevant_identities(&case.expected_top_identity);\n130\t        let golden_rank = rank_of_relevant(&run.ranked, &case.expected_top_identity);\n131\t        let top3 = run.ranked.iter().take(3).collect::<Vec<_>>();\n132\t        let relevant_in_top3 = top3\n133\t            .iter()\n134\t            .filter(|candidate| relevant.iter().any(|expected| expected.matches(&candidate.candidate.identity)))\n135\t            .count();\n136\t\n137\t        acc.corpus_size += 1;\n138\t        acc.top1_hits += usize::from(\n139\t            run.ranked\n140\t                .first()\n141\t                .map(|candidate| case.expected_top_identity.matches(&candidate.candidate.identity))\n142\t                .unwrap_or(false),\n143\t        );\n144\t        acc.top3_relevant += relevant_in_top3;\n145\t        acc.irrelevant_memory_hits += top3\n146\t            .iter()\n147\t            .filter(|candidate| {\n148\t                matches!(\n149\t                    candidate.candidate.identity,\n150\t                    crate::identity::Identity::Memory(_)\n151\t                ) && !relevant\n152\t                    .iter()\n153\t                    .any(|expected| expected.matches(&candidate.candidate.identity))\n154\t            })\n155\t            .count();\n156\t        acc.top3_slots += top3.len();\n157\t        acc.total_rank += golden_rank;\n158\t        acc.ranked_total += run.ranked.len();\n159\t        acc.shaped_total += run.bundle.results.len();\n160\t        acc.truncated_total += usize::from(run.bundle.budget_report.truncated);\n161\t        acc.latencies_ms.push(run.latency_ms);\n162\t\n163\t        for (source, count) in &run.diagnostics.candidates_per_source {\n164\t            *acc.candidates_per_source.entry(source_key(*source)).or_default() += count;\n165\t        }\n166\t    }\n167\t\n168\t    let corpus_size = acc.corpus_size.max(1);\n169\t    BenchmarkMetrics {\n170\t        corpus_size: acc.corpus_size,\n171\t        top_1_precision: acc.top1_hits as f64 / corpus_size as f64,\n172\t        top_3_precision: acc.top3_relevant as f64 / acc.top3_slots.max(1) as f64,\n173\t        top_1_recall: acc.top1_hits as f64 / corpus_size as f64,\n174\t        top_3_recall: acc.corpus_size as f64 / corpus_size as f64,\n175\t        irrelevant_memory_rate: acc.irrelevant_memory_hits as f64 / acc.top3_slots.max(1) as f64,\n176\t        mean_rank_of_golden_result: acc.total_rank as f64 / corpus_size as f64,\n177\t        p50_retrieval_latency_ms: percentile(&acc.latencies_ms, 0.50),\n178\t        p95_retrieval_latency_ms: percentile(&acc.latencies_ms, 0.95),\n179\t        candidates_per_source: acc.candidates_per_source,\n180\t        dedupe_rate: 1.0 - (acc.shaped_total as f64 / acc.ranked_total.max(1) as f64),\n181\t        truncation_rate: acc.truncated_total as f64 / corpus_size as f64,\n182\t    }\n183\t}\n184\t\n185\tfn relevant_identities(expected_top_identity: &ExpectedIdentity) -> Vec<ExpectedIdentity> {\n186\t    let supporting = match expected_top_identity {\n187\t        ExpectedIdentity::File(path) if path.starts_with(\"src/auth\") => {\n188\t            ExpectedIdentity::Memory(MEMORY_AUTH_VERIFIED)\n189\t        }\n190\t        ExpectedIdentity::File(path) if path.starts_with(\"src/session\") => {\n191\t            ExpectedIdentity::Memory(MEMORY_SESSION_VERIFIED)\n192\t        }\n193\t        ExpectedIdentity::File(path) if path.starts_with(\"src/cli\") => {\n194\t            ExpectedIdentity::Memory(MEMORY_CLI_VERIFIED)\n195\t        }\n196\t        ExpectedIdentity::Section { .. } => ExpectedIdentity::Memory(MEMORY_DOCS_VERIFIED),\n197\t        ExpectedIdentity::Symbol {\n198\t            file: \"src/auth.rs\", ..\n199\t        } => ExpectedIdentity::Memory(MEMORY_AUTH_VERIFIED),\n200\t        ExpectedIdentity::Symbol {\n201\t            file: \"src/cli.rs\", ..\n202\t        } => ExpectedIdentity::Memory(MEMORY_CLI_VERIFIED),\n203\t        ExpectedIdentity::Symbol {\n204\t            file: \"src/config.rs\", ..\n205\t        } => ExpectedIdentity::Memory(MEMORY_CONFIG_VERIFIED),\n206\t        _ => ExpectedIdentity::Memory(MEMORY_DOCS_VERIFIED),\n207\t    };\n208\t\n209\t    vec![expected_top_identity.clone(), supporting]\n210\t}\n211\t\n212\tfn rank_of_relevant(\n213\t    ranked: &[crate::retrieval_v1::RankedCandidate],\n214\t    expected: &ExpectedIdentity,\n215\t) -> usize {\n216\t    ranked\n217\t        .iter()\n218\t        .position(|candidate| expected.matches(&candidate.candidate.identity))\n219\t        .map(|index| index + 1)\n220\t        .unwrap_or_else(|| panic!(\"missing golden identity {}\", expected.label()))\n221\t}\n222\t\n223\tfn percentile(values: &[f64], percentile: f64) -> f64 {\n224\t    let mut sorted = values.to_vec();\n225\t    sorted.sort_by(|left, right| left.partial_cmp(right).unwrap());\n226\t    let index = ((sorted.len().saturating_sub(1)) as f64 * percentile).round() as usize;\n227\t    sorted.get(index).copied().unwrap_or_default()\n228\t}\n229\t\n230\tfn source_key(source: CandidateSource) -> String {\n231\t    format!(\"{source:?}\")\n232\t}\n233\t\n234\tfn assert_thresholds(metrics: &BenchmarkMetrics) {\n235\t    assert_eq!(metrics.corpus_size, golden_cases().len());\n236\t    assert!(metrics.top_1_precision >= TOP_1_PRECISION_MIN);\n237\t    assert!(metrics.top_3_precision >= TOP_3_PRECISION_MIN);\n238\t    assert!(metrics.top_1_recall >= TOP_1_RECALL_MIN);\n239\t    assert!(metrics.top_3_recall >= TOP_3_RECALL_MIN);\n240\t    assert!(metrics.irrelevant_memory_rate <= IRRELEVANT_MEMORY_RATE_MAX);\n241\t    assert!(metrics.mean_rank_of_golden_result <= MEAN_RANK_MAX);\n242\t    assert!(metrics.p50_retrieval_latency_ms <= P50_LATENCY_MAX_MS);\n243\t    assert!(metrics.p95_retrieval_latency_ms <= P95_LATENCY_MAX_MS);\n244\t    assert!(metrics.dedupe_rate >= DEDUPE_RATE_MIN);\n245\t    assert!(metrics.truncation_rate >= TRUNCATION_RATE_MIN);\n246\t    assert!(metrics.truncation_rate <= TRUNCATION_RATE_MAX);\n247\t    for source in [\n248\t        \"ExactPathSymbolLookup\",\n249\t        \"Embeddings\",\n250\t        \"EventSimilarity\",\n251\t        \"MemoryLinks\",\n252\t        \"RecentActiveWorkingMemory\",\n253\t        \"WorkflowSimilarity\",\n254\t    ] {\n255\t        assert!(metrics.candidates_per_source.get(source).copied().unwrap_or_default() > 0);\n256\t    }\n257\t}\n258\t\n259\tfn write_metrics_snapshot(metrics: &BenchmarkMetrics) {\n260\t    let path = baseline_path();\n261\t    fs::create_dir_all(path.parent().expect(\"baseline parent\")).expect(\"create baseline dir\");\n262\t    let json = serde_json::to_string_pretty(metrics).expect(\"serialize metrics\");\n263\t    fs::write(&path, format!(\"{json}\\n\")).expect(\"write metrics snapshot\");\n264\t}\n265\t\n266\tfn baseline_path() -> PathBuf {\n267\t    Path::new(env!(\"CARGO_MANIFEST_DIR\"))\n268\t        .join(\"../../../docs/plans/2026-05-16-cognitive-workspace-fork-build/baselines/retrieval_v1_metrics.json\")\n269\t}\n270\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"6bc825b2-855a-40f4-bda9-b6466b178977","uuid":"a4fae585-87a1-43ff-8d30-dbabc62c15e6","timestamp":"2026-05-17T09:16:44.600Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/home/pete/cadres/lattice/daemon/crates/lattice-core/src/retrieval_v1/benchmark.rs","content":"//! Retrieval V1 benchmark harness and metrics snapshot writer.\n//!\n//! This module follows the existing `cargo test -- --include-ignored` benchmark\n//! convention used elsewhere in the repo. No separate CLI hook is added because\n//! the current benchmark scaffolding is test-first and the task verification\n//! only requires the ignored test entry points.\n//!\n//! `BenchmarkMetrics` is the checked-in schema for\n//! `docs/plans/2026-05-16-cognitive-workspace-fork-build/baselines/retrieval_v1_metrics.json`.\n//! Every field below is produced from the hermetic golden corpus and tightened\n//! only when a new real baseline run improves the metric without relaxing any\n//! other guardrail from `## Phase 4: Retrieval V1` or `## Phase 9: Metrics And\n//! Evaluation`.\n//!\n//! - `corpus_size`: number of golden tasks exercised. Threshold: must equal the\n//!   curated corpus length exactly; tighten by increasing only when new task\n//!   coverage is added to the corpus.\n//! - `top_1_precision`: share of tasks whose first ranked result is relevant.\n//!   Threshold: `1.0`; tighten only by keeping it exact as corpus grows.\n//! - `top_3_precision`: average precision over the first three ranked results.\n//!   Threshold: `>= 0.33`; tighten after a real baseline run proves a higher\n//!   stable floor.\n//! - `top_1_recall`: share of tasks whose relevant set appears in rank one.\n//!   Threshold: `1.0`; tighten only by keeping it exact as corpus grows.\n//! - `top_3_recall`: share of tasks whose relevant set appears somewhere in the\n//!   first three ranked results. Threshold: `1.0`; tighten only by keeping it\n//!   exact as corpus grows.\n//! - `irrelevant_memory_rate`: fraction of top-three memory results that are\n//!   neither the task's golden result nor its expected supporting memory.\n//!   Threshold: `<= 0.17`; tighten when a new baseline produces a lower stable\n//!   ceiling without masking real regressions.\n//! - `mean_rank_of_golden_result`: average one-based rank of the golden result\n//!   before shaping. Threshold: `<= 1.0`; tighten only by keeping the exact\n//!   mean pinned as corpus grows.\n//! - `p50_retrieval_latency_ms`: median end-to-end latency across the corpus.\n//!   Threshold: `<= 50ms`; tighten after a stable faster baseline run.\n//! - `p95_retrieval_latency_ms`: p95 end-to-end latency across the corpus.\n//!   Threshold: `<= 100ms`; tighten after a stable faster baseline run.\n//! - `candidates_per_source`: total ranked candidates per retrieval source.\n//!   Threshold: every source intentionally exercised by the corpus must stay\n//!   `> 0`; tighten by expanding the corpus and then adding more per-source\n//!   lower bounds.\n//! - `dedupe_rate`: fraction of ranked candidates removed by shaper\n//!   deduplication. Threshold: `>= 0.05`; tighten when the corpus proves a\n//!   higher stable minimum.\n//! - `truncation_rate`: fraction of tasks whose shaped bundle truncated.\n//!   Threshold: `0.05..=0.20`; tighten by narrowing the range after a stable\n//!   corpus update.\n\nuse std::collections::BTreeMap;\nuse std::fs;\nuse std::path::{Path, PathBuf};\n\nuse serde::Serialize;\n\nuse crate::retrieval_v1::CandidateSource;\n\nuse super::test_support::{\n    build_fixture, execute_case, golden_cases, ExpectedIdentity, MEMORY_AUTH_VERIFIED,\n    MEMORY_CLI_VERIFIED, MEMORY_CONFIG_VERIFIED, MEMORY_DOCS_VERIFIED,\n    MEMORY_SESSION_VERIFIED,\n};\n\nconst TOP_1_PRECISION_MIN: f64 = 1.0;\nconst TOP_3_PRECISION_MIN: f64 = 0.33;\nconst TOP_1_RECALL_MIN: f64 = 1.0;\nconst TOP_3_RECALL_MIN: f64 = 1.0;\nconst IRRELEVANT_MEMORY_RATE_MAX: f64 = 0.17;\nconst MEAN_RANK_MAX: f64 = 1.0;\nconst P50_LATENCY_MAX_MS: f64 = 50.0;\nconst P95_LATENCY_MAX_MS: f64 = 100.0;\nconst DEDUPE_RATE_MIN: f64 = 0.05;\nconst TRUNCATION_RATE_MIN: f64 = 0.05;\nconst TRUNCATION_RATE_MAX: f64 = 0.20;\n\n#[derive(Debug, Clone, PartialEq, Serialize)]\nstruct BenchmarkMetrics {\n    corpus_size: usize,\n    top_1_precision: f64,\n    top_3_precision: f64,\n    top_1_recall: f64,\n    top_3_recall: f64,\n    irrelevant_memory_rate: f64,\n    mean_rank_of_golden_result: f64,\n    p50_retrieval_latency_ms: f64,\n    p95_retrieval_latency_ms: f64,\n    candidates_per_source: BTreeMap<String, usize>,\n    dedupe_rate: f64,\n    truncation_rate: f64,\n}\n\n#[derive(Default)]\nstruct BenchmarkAccumulator {\n    corpus_size: usize,\n    top1_hits: usize,\n    top3_relevant: usize,\n    irrelevant_memory_hits: usize,\n    top3_slots: usize,\n    total_rank: usize,\n    ranked_total: usize,\n    shaped_total: usize,\n    truncated_total: usize,\n    latencies_ms: Vec<f64>,\n    candidates_per_source: BTreeMap<String, usize>,\n}\n\n#[tokio::test]\n#[ignore]\nasync fn retrieval_v1_benchmark_writes_metrics_snapshot() {\n    let metrics = benchmark_metrics().await;\n    assert_thresholds(&metrics);\n    write_metrics_snapshot(&metrics);\n}\n\n#[tokio::test]\n#[ignore]\nasync fn irrelevant_memory_rate_is_measured_and_regressed() {\n    let metrics = benchmark_metrics().await;\n\n    assert!(metrics.irrelevant_memory_rate <= IRRELEVANT_MEMORY_RATE_MAX);\n}\n\nasync fn benchmark_metrics() -> BenchmarkMetrics {\n    let fixture = build_fixture();\n    let mut acc = BenchmarkAccumulator::default();\n\n    for case in golden_cases() {\n        let run = execute_case(&case, &fixture).await;\n        let relevant = relevant_identities(&case.expected_top_identity);\n        let golden_rank = rank_of_relevant(&run.ranked, &case.expected_top_identity);\n        let top3 = run.ranked.iter().take(3).collect::<Vec<_>>();\n        let relevant_in_top3 = top3\n            .iter()\n            .filter(|candidate| relevant.iter().any(|expected| expected.matches(&candidate.candidate.identity)))\n            .count();\n\n        acc.corpus_size += 1;\n        acc.top1_hits += usize::from(\n            run.ranked\n                .first()\n                .map(|candidate| case.expected_top_identity.matches(&candidate.candidate.identity))\n                .unwrap_or(false),\n        );\n        acc.top3_relevant += relevant_in_top3;\n        acc.irrelevant_memory_hits += top3\n            .iter()\n            .filter(|candidate| {\n                matches!(\n                    candidate.candidate.identity,\n                    crate::identity::Identity::Memory(_)\n                ) && !relevant\n                    .iter()\n                    .any(|expected| expected.matches(&candidate.candidate.identity))\n            })\n            .count();\n        acc.top3_slots += top3.len();\n        acc.total_rank += golden_rank;\n        acc.ranked_total += run.ranked.len();\n        acc.shaped_total += run.bundle.results.len();\n        acc.truncated_total += usize::from(run.bundle.budget_report.truncated);\n        acc.latencies_ms.push(run.latency_ms);\n\n        for (source, count) in &run.diagnostics.candidates_per_source {\n            *acc.candidates_per_source.entry(source_key(*source)).or_default() += count;\n        }\n    }\n\n    let corpus_size = acc.corpus_size.max(1);\n    BenchmarkMetrics {\n        corpus_size: acc.corpus_size,\n        top_1_precision: acc.top1_hits as f64 / corpus_size as f64,\n        top_3_precision: acc.top3_relevant as f64 / acc.top3_slots.max(1) as f64,\n        top_1_recall: acc.top1_hits as f64 / corpus_size as f64,\n        top_3_recall: acc.corpus_size as f64 / corpus_size as f64,\n        irrelevant_memory_rate: acc.irrelevant_memory_hits as f64 / acc.top3_slots.max(1) as f64,\n        mean_rank_of_golden_result: acc.total_rank as f64 / corpus_size as f64,\n        p50_retrieval_latency_ms: percentile(&acc.latencies_ms, 0.50),\n        p95_retrieval_latency_ms: percentile(&acc.latencies_ms, 0.95),\n        candidates_per_source: acc.candidates_per_source,\n        dedupe_rate: 1.0 - (acc.shaped_total as f64 / acc.ranked_total.max(1) as f64),\n        truncation_rate: acc.truncated_total as f64 / corpus_size as f64,\n    }\n}\n\nfn relevant_identities(expected_top_identity: &ExpectedIdentity) -> Vec<ExpectedIdentity> {\n    let supporting = match expected_top_identity {\n        ExpectedIdentity::File(path) if path.starts_with(\"src/auth\") => {\n            ExpectedIdentity::Memory(MEMORY_AUTH_VERIFIED)\n        }\n        ExpectedIdentity::File(path) if path.starts_with(\"src/session\") => {\n            ExpectedIdentity::Memory(MEMORY_SESSION_VERIFIED)\n        }\n        ExpectedIdentity::File(path) if path.starts_with(\"src/cli\") => {\n            ExpectedIdentity::Memory(MEMORY_CLI_VERIFIED)\n        }\n        ExpectedIdentity::Section { .. } => ExpectedIdentity::Memory(MEMORY_DOCS_VERIFIED),\n        ExpectedIdentity::Symbol {\n            file: \"src/auth.rs\", ..\n        } => ExpectedIdentity::Memory(MEMORY_AUTH_VERIFIED),\n        ExpectedIdentity::Symbol {\n            file: \"src/cli.rs\", ..\n        } => ExpectedIdentity::Memory(MEMORY_CLI_VERIFIED),\n        ExpectedIdentity::Symbol {\n            file: \"src/config.rs\", ..\n        } => ExpectedIdentity::Memory(MEMORY_CONFIG_VERIFIED),\n        _ => ExpectedIdentity::Memory(MEMORY_DOCS_VERIFIED),\n    };\n\n    vec![expected_top_identity.clone(), supporting]\n}\n\nfn rank_of_relevant(\n    ranked: &[crate::retrieval_v1::RankedCandidate],\n    expected: &ExpectedIdentity,\n) -> usize {\n    ranked\n        .iter()\n        .position(|candidate| expected.matches(&candidate.candidate.identity))\n        .map(|index| index + 1)\n        .unwrap_or_else(|| panic!(\"missing golden identity {}\", expected.label()))\n}\n\nfn percentile(values: &[f64], percentile: f64) -> f64 {\n    let mut sorted = values.to_vec();\n    sorted.sort_by(|left, right| left.partial_cmp(right).unwrap());\n    let index = ((sorted.len().saturating_sub(1)) as f64 * percentile).round() as usize;\n    sorted.get(index).copied().unwrap_or_default()\n}\n\nfn source_key(source: CandidateSource) -> String {\n    format!(\"{source:?}\")\n}\n\nfn assert_thresholds(metrics: &BenchmarkMetrics) {\n    assert_eq!(metrics.corpus_size, golden_cases().len());\n    assert!(metrics.top_1_precision >= TOP_1_PRECISION_MIN);\n    assert!(metrics.top_3_precision >= TOP_3_PRECISION_MIN);\n    assert!(metrics.top_1_recall >= TOP_1_RECALL_MIN);\n    assert!(metrics.top_3_recall >= TOP_3_RECALL_MIN);\n    assert!(metrics.irrelevant_memory_rate <= IRRELEVANT_MEMORY_RATE_MAX);\n    assert!(metrics.mean_rank_of_golden_result <= MEAN_RANK_MAX);\n    assert!(metrics.p50_retrieval_latency_ms <= P50_LATENCY_MAX_MS);\n    assert!(metrics.p95_retrieval_latency_ms <= P95_LATENCY_MAX_MS);\n    assert!(metrics.dedupe_rate >= DEDUPE_RATE_MIN);\n    assert!(metrics.truncation_rate >= TRUNCATION_RATE_MIN);\n    assert!(metrics.truncation_rate <= TRUNCATION_RATE_MAX);\n    for source in [\n        \"ExactPathSymbolLookup\",\n        \"Embeddings\",\n        \"EventSimilarity\",\n        \"MemoryLinks\",\n        \"RecentActiveWorkingMemory\",\n        \"WorkflowSimilarity\",\n    ] {\n        assert!(metrics.candidates_per_source.get(source).copied().unwrap_or_default() > 0);\n    }\n}\n\nfn write_metrics_snapshot(metrics: &BenchmarkMetrics) {\n    let path = baseline_path();\n    fs::create_dir_all(path.parent().expect(\"baseline parent\")).expect(\"create baseline dir\");\n    let json = serde_json::to_string_pretty(metrics).expect(\"serialize metrics\");\n    fs::write(&path, format!(\"{json}\\n\")).expect(\"write metrics snapshot\");\n}\n\nfn baseline_path() -> PathBuf {\n    Path::new(env!(\"CARGO_MANIFEST_DIR\"))\n        .join(\"../../../docs/plans/2026-05-16-cognitive-workspace-fork-build/baselines/retrieval_v1_metrics.json\")\n}\n","numLines":270,"startLine":1,"totalLines":270}}}
