{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01BR7RU5FzE7wq9xRjrwd5jC","type":"tool_result","content":"907\t### Ranking Complexity\n908\t\n909\tRisk: ranking becomes hard to reason about.\n910\t\n911\tControl: keep ranker feature-based and inspectable before any learned policy. Expose diagnostic scores.\n912\t\n913\t### Event Log Growth\n914\t\n915\tRisk: event storage becomes too large or slow.\n916\t\n917\tControl: append compact summaries on hot paths, spill large payloads, index by task/session/workspace, and support compaction snapshots.\n918\t\n919\t### Stale Memory Leakage\n920\t\n921\tRisk: agents trust outdated memory.\n922\t\n923\tControl: freshness indexes, graph-change-triggered verification, stale labels in all memory surfaces, and tests that stale memory cannot rank as trusted.\n924\t\n925\t### Scope Leakage\n926\t\n927\tRisk: user/org/branch memories leak into wrong workspaces.\n928\t\n929\tControl: scope-aware queries, enforced filters in store APIs, and negative tests.\n930\t\n931\t### Overfitting To Current Repo\n932\t\n933\tRisk: benchmarks pass only for Lattice-like Rust/TypeScript repos.\n934\t\n935\tControl: fixture repos across languages, repo sizes, and documentation styles.\n936\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"6bc825b2-855a-40f4-bda9-b6466b178977","uuid":"58ed6151-3e6a-468c-9d6a-6666c6911f8d","timestamp":"2026-05-17T09:21:09.398Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/home/pete/cadres/lattice/docs/plans/2026-05-16-cognitive-workspace-fork-plan.md","content":"### Ranking Complexity\n\nRisk: ranking becomes hard to reason about.\n\nControl: keep ranker feature-based and inspectable before any learned policy. Expose diagnostic scores.\n\n### Event Log Growth\n\nRisk: event storage becomes too large or slow.\n\nControl: append compact summaries on hot paths, spill large payloads, index by task/session/workspace, and support compaction snapshots.\n\n### Stale Memory Leakage\n\nRisk: agents trust outdated memory.\n\nControl: freshness indexes, graph-change-triggered verification, stale labels in all memory surfaces, and tests that stale memory cannot rank as trusted.\n\n### Scope Leakage\n\nRisk: user/org/branch memories leak into wrong workspaces.\n\nControl: scope-aware queries, enforced filters in store APIs, and negative tests.\n\n### Overfitting To Current Repo\n\nRisk: benchmarks pass only for Lattice-like Rust/TypeScript repos.\n\nControl: fixture repos across languages, repo sizes, and documentation styles.\n","numLines":30,"startLine":907,"totalLines":969}}}
